Appendix G: Parameter Calibration

G.1 Null-Run Calibration

Thresholds \theta_B, \theta_A, h are calibrated on null runs with no known divergence events:

\theta_B = \operatorname{Quantile}_{0.90}\left(\{\mathcal{D}(t)\}_{\text{null}}\right), \quad \theta_A = \operatorname{Quantile}_{0.99}\left(\{\mathcal{D}(t)\}_{\text{null}}\right)

G.2 Operationalization of Effort and Effectiveness

Effort:

I_{\text{effort}}(t) = w_1 \cdot \frac{\text{safety fine-tuning compute}}{\text{total compute}} + w_2 \cdot \frac{\text{red-team budget}}{\text{total budget}} + w_3 \cdot \Delta A_{\text{monitor}}

Effectiveness:

E_{\text{safety}}(t) = \mathbb{E}\left[\frac{|\mathcal{D}(t)| - |\mathcal{D}(t-\tau)|}{|\mathcal{D}(t-\tau)|} \,\middle|\, I_{\text{effort}} > 0\right]

estimated via a windowed regression. This is a latent quantity with its own uncertainty, and we acknowledge that its identification requires sufficient intervention events.

