Appendix H: Retrospective Test Protocol

H.1 Pre-Registered Analysis Plan

1. Define proxies for C(t) and Q_A(t) from public benchmarks and system cards.
2. Pre-register predictions: e.g., "\mathcal{D}_{\text{monitor}}(t) becomes positive between generations."
3. Compute \mathcal{D}_{\text{monitor}}, \mathcal{D}_{\text{eval}}, \mathcal{D}_{\text{confidence}}.
4. Test whether structural change \Delta\Sigma_t precedes marginal degradation.
5. Report false negatives and false positives.

H.2 Falsification Conditions

1. If Q_A(t) does not decrease when evaluation awareness increases, the uncertainty penalty term is invalid.
2. If \boldsymbol{\Sigma}(t) shows no structural change during known divergence events, H1 is falsified.
3. If debt B(t) grows unboundedly in runs post-hoc assessed as safe, the debt model is over-sensitive.
4. If conclusions are not robust across Q_A^{\text{prod}} and Q_A^{\text{min}}, the conjunctive-composition assumption is insufficient.

H.3 Simulation Study

Synthetic trajectories with known degradation events:

C(t) = \log(t), \quad A_{\text{monitor}}(t) = \frac{1}{1 + 0.1t}

Inject controlled covariance shifts at known times and measure detection latency across marginal-only, covariance-only, and combined monitoring. Covariance shift magnitudes: \Delta\rho \in \{0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7\}. ARL target: \text{ARL}_0 = 1000.

