    │                                                                                              │
    │     Conflating levels produces category errors:                                              │
    │       • Level 1 ≠ Level 2: "the benchmark says X" ≠ "X is true"                              │
    │       • Level 2 ≠ Level 3: "the estimate is X" ≠ "the derived quantity means Y"              │
    │       • Level 3 ≠ safety: "assurance quality is high" ≠ "the system is safe"                 │
    │                                                                                              │
    │     ADD operates strictly at Levels 1→2→3.                                                   │
    │     ADD never claims to measure safety directly.                                             │
